# Mealvana Endurance – Cursor Rules

## TL;DR
- Flutter + Riverpod v2 + Hive + Supabase with Feature-Oriented Architecture (FOA).
- Controllers MUST be `@riverpod` `AsyncNotifier`-based with codegen and `AsyncValue.guard`.
- All UI text and algorithm parameters come from `ContentService` (no hardcoded strings or magic numbers).
- Offline-first: write to Hive first; backend is secondary. Provide safe fallbacks.

## Non‑Negotiables
- Architecture: Follow Andrea Bizzotto FOA with four layers per feature: `presentation/`, `application/`, `domain/`, `data/`.
- Controllers: Use `@riverpod` classes extending `AsyncNotifier<T>` (never `StateNotifier`, never manual providers).
  - Include `part '<file>.g.dart';`
  - Access services via `ref.read(...)`
  - Initialize with a synchronous `build()` returning initial state
  - Use `AsyncValue.guard` for async ops and `ref.invalidateSelf()` for refresh
- Content: All user-facing strings and algorithm parameters must be read via `ContentService` and `ContentKeys`.
  - Fallback order: Supabase → Hive cache → bundled defaults (`assets/config/content_defaults.json`)
  - Do not hardcode UI text or algorithm constants
- Offline-first/Hive: Persist locally first; design for no-network scenarios.
  - Use encrypted Hive for sensitive data
  - Maintain snake_case in storage, camelCase in Dart
- Error handling: Use `AsyncValue.guard`, don’t swallow errors, expose UI via standard snackbar helpers
- Type safety: Strongly typed models; avoid `dynamic`/`any` patterns
- Do not introduce static methods for DI; always wire via Riverpod providers

## File/Module Boundaries
- Place code under `lib/features/<feature>/{presentation,application,domain,data}`
- Cross-feature calls go through `application` services wired by providers; presentation never reaches directly into `data`
- Shared utilities/widgets live under `lib/shared/`

## Controller Template
Use this exact pattern when adding controllers:
```dart
import 'dart:async';
import 'package:riverpod_annotation/riverpod_annotation.dart';
import '../../content/application/content_service.dart';
import '../../content/domain/content_keys.dart';

part 'screen_controller.g.dart';

@riverpod
class ScreenController extends _$ScreenController {
	ContentService get _content => ref.read(contentServiceProvider);
	MyService get _service => ref.read(myServiceProvider);

	@override
	FutureOr<ScreenState> build() {
		final titleFuture = _content.getValue(ContentKeys.screenTitle, defaultValue: 'Title');
		return ScreenState.initial(titleFuture);
	}

	Future<void> performAction() async {
		state = const AsyncLoading();
		state = await AsyncValue.guard(() async {
			final result = await _service.doWork();
			return state.requireValue.copyWith(result: result);
		});
	}

	Future<void> refresh() async {
		await _service.refresh();
		ref.invalidateSelf();
	}
}
```

## ContentService Usage
- Keys must be defined in `ContentKeys` and have defaults in `assets/config/content_defaults.json`.
- Read UI strings:
```dart
final title = await ref.read(contentServiceProvider)
	.getValue(ContentKeys.mainScreenTitle, defaultValue: 'Mealvana Endurance');
```
- Read algorithm params:
```dart
final minCarbs = await ref.read(contentServiceProvider)
	.getAlgorithmParameter('during_run.carbs.absorption_limit_min_g_per_h', defaultValue: 30.0);
```
- Read nested categories:
```dart
final multipliers = await ref.read(contentServiceProvider)
	.getAlgorithmCategory('during_run.carbs.gut_training_multipliers');
```

## Data & Storage
- Boxes: `user_profiles`, `food_preferences`, `nutrition_plans`, `content_box`, `feedback`, `meta`
- Local-first writes; add soft-deletes where applicable
- Encrypted boxes for sensitive data
- Prefer repositories for IO; keep mapping consistent: snake_case in storage, camelCase in Dart

## Navigation & UI
- Use `go_router` for navigation; keep UI layer dumb (no business logic in widgets)
- Follow theming under `lib/theme/` and shared widgets under `lib/shared/widgets/`

## Analytics & Monitoring
- Use `lib/services/analytics_service.dart` or `lib/shared/services/analytics_service.dart` abstractions
- Track content source when relevant (backend|cache|default)
- Integrate Sentry for error reporting via shared services when available

## Build/Run/Test Commands
- Codegen (MANDATORY after adding/updating `@riverpod`, Hive adapters, etc.):
```bash
flutter pub run build_runner watch --delete-conflicting-outputs
# or one-time
flutter pub run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs
```
- Lint/Analyze:
```bash
flutter analyze
```
- Tests:
```bash
flutter test
```
- Run app:
```bash
flutter run
```

## Supabase
- Access via `supabase_flutter`
- Keys/URLs should use envs/dart-define for production; avoid committing secrets
- Tables: `app_content`, `user_profiles`, `nutrition_plans`, `feedback`

## Performance & Lifecycle
- Providers: default to `autoDispose` unless persistence is required
- Cache content for session; allow manual refresh; avoid blocking UI on network
- Clamp algorithm outputs to safe physiological ranges (see docs/business_logic)

## Adding Features – Checklist
1. Create feature folders under `lib/features/<name>/`
2. Define domain models and repositories (data layer)
3. Implement application services that orchestrate logic
4. Add `@riverpod` `AsyncNotifier` controllers (presentation)
5. Use `ContentService` for all strings/params; add missing keys + defaults
6. Write unit/widget tests; run `flutter test` and `flutter analyze`
7. Run codegen; verify no analyzer errors

## Style & Naming
- Dart: PascalCase for types, camelCase for fields; storage/API: snake_case
- Prefer descriptive names; avoid abbreviations and 1–2 letter variables
- Keep functions small with early returns; avoid deep nesting

## Do Not
- Do not use `StateNotifier` or manual providers
- Do not hardcode UI text or algorithm constants
- Do not perform data access in widgets
- Do not introduce static singletons for services; use providers
- Do not block UI on network or content fetching

